Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Required formal check: validate the producer's runtime
 fields, not only its hash

bind_receipt() checked the receipt's commit, repository, run id, status, effect,
manifest digest and log hashes, and nothing about the runtime it claims. It now
also requires, failing closed when a field is missing, malformed or stale:
- workflow_run_attempt equal to this run's GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT;
- lean_version fully matching Lean 4.34.1, commit 5045d005, Release;
- dependency_revisions equal to the bound manifest's exact 40-hex lock;
- dependency_worktrees == CLEAN;
- preflight and final observations, each with exactly those runtime fields,
  equal to each other, the final one equal to the receipt's version and
  manifest digest.
Historical receipts are not re-validated; the aggregate step is unchanged.

The fixture now carries a realistic receipt and lock. The attempt-identity test
records the producer attempt alongside the context, as the binder now requires.
ProducerRuntimeTests: on the previous binder all nine refusal controls fail
(27 subtests) while the valid record still binds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
